      "content": "<h3>1. push(E item)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>E push(E item)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the item that was pushed</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1) amortised</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Puts the item on the <strong>top</strong> of the stack. It also returns the item, which is handy in expressions.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Internally it calls <code>addElement(item)</code>, so the \"top\" is the <strong>last index</strong> of the underlying array (the opposite of <code>Deque.push</code>, which adds at the <em>front</em>). The vector grows by doubling when it is full.</p>",
