      "content": "<h3>5. search(Object o)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>int search(Object o)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> the 1-based distance from the top, or <code>-1</code></li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(n)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> Finds an element and tells how far it is from the <strong>top</strong>: the top element is at position <strong>1</strong>, the next at 2, and so on. If the element is not there you get <strong>-1</strong>. If it appears several times, the one <strong>closest to the top</strong> is reported.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> It is <code>size() - lastIndexOf(o)</code>. Note the two quirks: positions are <strong>1-based</strong> and counted <strong>from the top</strong>, unlike <code>indexOf</code> which is 0-based from the bottom.</p>",
